From d8f4c65dbd83609da5f74aeb8073421202075969 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:31:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] refactor(sim): a field carried between setups is the same
 field seen through the turn

#637 step A (M7.3): CarriedField views an SdfField through a setup
change's LatticeTurn - distance(p) = field.distance(T^-1 p), exact (a
signed distance is invariant under rigid motion), nothing re-sampled:
the field analogue of carry's "re-index, never re-sample". LatticeTurn
gains unapply (the exact inverse) and then (composition). Not yet used
by carry::Body (steps B-D).

Pinned by field_carry (3): unapply inverts apply and then composes for
all eight turns; a cut field reads bit-identical through every turn;
carrying twice equals carrying through the composed turn.

Refs #637

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
